# The PRESENCE of this file is the point: with an .npmignore, npm does NOT
# consult the repo .gitignore when packing. The root .gitignore ignores
# `packages/*/pkg/` (the wasm-pack build output), and some npm versions
# (node20 / npm 10 in CI) exclude gitignored paths from the tarball EVEN when
# listed in package.json "files" — which shipped an empty pkg/ and broke every
# consumer on `./pkg/skyfire_wasm.js` (rust-skyfire#76 follow-up).
#
# With this file present, the "files" allowlist alone governs the tarball, so
# the built pkg/ (WASM) ships. Do not delete. Add real exclusions below only if
# ever needed — "files" already restricts the tarball, so none are required.
